course: dictionary
lesson: 12433
title: Decelerate: slowing down
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To decelerate means to slow down, or to go less fast. It is the opposite of accelerate, which means to speed up. When you meet decelerate, look for clues in the words around it.
explain: «The car began to decelerate as the driver pressed the brake.» Brakes are there to slow a car, so decelerate must mean slow down. Check it: put "slow down" in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. It does.
explain: Decelerate is a verb, so its forms change: decelerates, decelerated, decelerating. The noun is deceleration. «The deceleration of the train made everyone lurch forward.» Here deceleration means the slowing down itself.
explain: Decelerate is a science and maths word too. A ball rolling on grass slows down because of friction, so it decelerates. In maths, deceleration means speed is getting smaller over time.
fact: Decelerate means to slow down, or to go less fast.
fact: Decelerate is a verb: decelerates, decelerated, decelerating. The noun is deceleration.
fact: Friction and air resistance can make objects decelerate.
fact: In maths, deceleration means speed is getting smaller over time.
fact: «The cyclist decelerated gently before the corner.» This means she slowed down smoothly.
exercise: «The train began to decelerate as it reached the station.» What does decelerate mean? | *To slow down | To go faster | To turn around
exercise: Which word is the noun for decelerate? | *deceleration | celebration | decelerating
exercise: In maths, what does deceleration mean? | The object is getting heavier | Distance is getting bigger over time | *Speed is getting smaller over time
test: «The ball rolling across the grass began to decelerate.» What can make a rolling ball decelerate? | A hot sun | *Friction | A bright colour
test: Ella's dad says, «I need to decelerate before the speed bump.» What does he need to do? | Jump out of the car | *Slow down | Speed up
exam: Which sentence uses decelerate correctly? | The kettle decelerated, so the cupboard was painted green. | The lamp decelerated its brightness into a song. | *The runner decelerated as she reached the finish line and jogged to a stop.
